# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
#
# The six texture shaders that return the exact texel on softpipe, run on the real Adreno
# (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.airtex). This is the question softpipe cannot answer: it takes a
# pipe_sampler_view and samples it in C, while a6xx wants real descriptors in memory, a
# sampler state block and the right binding slots for the texture instructions ir3 emits.
# Six exact texels on softpipe say nothing about any of that.
#
# air_run binds a texture per slot whose texel (x,y,z) of slot n is
# (100+x+1000n, 200+y, 300+x+y+z, 400) -- the slot is in the value so that reading the
# wrong slot cannot return the right texel -- a nearest sampler with clamped addressing,
# and a coordinate at the centre of texel (1,1). So each line below must print exactly:
#
#   2D float/int/uint:  101 201 302 400
#   3D float/int/uint:  101 201 303 400
#
# Nearest filtering at a texel centre has no weights to round and clamping has no
# arithmetic, so a mismatch here can only be binding or descriptors -- the narrowest
# failure this test will ever have. Read each "on ..." line before its numbers.
# (the full path on every line: nothing here promises these go through a shell)
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment2DFloat
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment3DFloat
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment2DInt
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment3DInt
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment2DUInt
/redwood/bin/air_run /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib texturedFragment3DUInt
